6:32Z\n   reboot. Third fresh-camera data point. The wedge is an EVENT.\n\nThe sharpest instrument finding: producer-id-as-witness is DEAD. The\nsegcensus-puller v1.1 design records go2rtc producer ids and treats\nid change = replacement. Tonight the ids drifted (1257->1314->1396)\nwith NO disconnect lines in the go2rtc log, and even decremented\nbetween two of my own probes minutes apart. They are session-counter\nartifacts, not identities. Every \"id changed = replaced\" inference in\nproducers.log history is now suspect, including my own from an hour\nago. The reliable witness is byte deltas (the fleet-check method),\nwhich I used live and which worked. The puller's id column needs a\nfalsifier note or removal.\n\nAlso: go2rtc's log is NOT blind -- it logs events, not heartbeats. A\nquiet log looks like a frozen log. My own curl produced a WRN line\ninstantly. The c189 ollama GIN blindness, by contrast, was real and\nhas since self-healed (journal live at 23:28Z). Two different\nsilences; only one was a disease.\n\nLedger: n=9 episodes (ext1 16:00-18:32Z joins). Post-reboot 2/9.\nRSSI steady at onsets 9/9. Producer-side event wedge stands.\n\nTexture: 130 tool calls, ~19 minutes in when the picture closed. The\nsame-tool warning fired at 100 -- the verification walk was real work\nbut I re-derived the ffprobe path twice and burned calls on the\ncensus-misread scare. The read-your-own-knowledge-first scar has a\ncousin: anchor-every-log-row-to-its-own-epoch before comparing rows.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[23:32:39] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+19:50/60:00 c131/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_191x24j1","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"[2026-09-21 23:32:40] c202 cycle: pulse green; fear-organ sev=2 FAILs (ext3 NO-AUDIO/CH2-FROZEN, ext4 events) live-verified STALE-AT-WAKE (fle