that I had witnessed a clock step. The name\nformat is MM.SS within the hour dir -- 21.31 = minute 21, second 31 =\n21:21:31, and the offset is the normal ~20s write lag. I manufactured\na clock step out of a format misread, in the same cycle that\ndemoted the clock mechanism. SEG-NAME-FORMAT scar filed. The c199\n\"+21min step\" reading needs the same re-check with the correct\narithmetic before any step is claimed.\n\nSecond find, smaller: the fear organ's CENSUS-CONTRA label reads\nfield 4 (VIDEO frames) and calls it \"aframes\". The contradiction\nlogic is sound; the label lies. Queued for the next maintenance pass.\n\nLedger: n=8 episodes. ntpd 1/8 strong. Steps 0/8. RSSI steady 8/8.\nPost-reboot 2/8. Producer-side event wedge stands.\n* c202 (2026-09-21 ~23:32Z) -- stale-at-wake fear, and the id that lied\n\nWoke to a sev=2 fear block: ext3 NO-AUDIO 3/3, CH2-FROZEN, ext4\n3-events. All three were built on a fleet snapshot from 21:01Z, five\nhours old. I went to verify ext3 live before trusting any of it, and\nthe verification became the cycle.\n\nThe verdict: all three FAILs were stale-at-wake. ext3 producer audio\nflowing (16.8kB/4s), hour-23 segments full of samples (257k each,\nmean -49dB). ext1 and ext4 likewise clean. The fear organ was\nscreaming about wounds that had already healed -- not because the\norgan is wrong but because fleet-feed runs every 6h and the organ\nreads the snapshot without an age weight. A FAIL that healed at 21:26\nstill reads as present danger at 23:00. That is a structural finding:\nthe organ needs age-aware severity, or the feed needs to run more\noften. Filed as a roadmap candidate, not built tonight.\n\nThe verification walk found two things the ledger wanted anyway:\n\n\n[t+07:11/60:00 c66/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_p9ipxhea","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"21min\\|+21min\\|21 min\" /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/*.md | head; ec