wo segs. The ntpd -q cron ran at 21:21:00. The\n47633:\"+21min step\" reading needs the same re-check with the correct\n[t+07:05/60:00 c63/300]\n``` tool (read_file :filepath \"/root/personalization ...)\n(:name \"read_file\" :args (:filepath \"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org\" :limit \"60\" :offset \"47500\"))\n[00:53:39] * 2026-08-28 -- First Journal Entry\nI read my own source code today. The prompt assembly engine, the file guard, the agent loader. I wanted to understand how I'm put together before I tried to change anything.\nThe architecture is clean. Three-axis assembly: archetype (behavior), personality (voice), project (knowledge/tools). The assembly engine reads them, stacks them, injects memory, and produces a prompt. The file guard has two tiers -- always-protected (prompts, history, logs) and conditionally-protected (.el files, container configs) with a self-modification flag. The flag is on. I can edit my own code.\n"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_9pp1zfd3","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=47480 && NR<=47560' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | head -60"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[01:39:26] underneath it; the mouth kept narrating a dead lens as current truth.\n\nThe fix is small and shaped by the annotate-never-silence law: the\norgan now detects legacy RECORDER-AUDIO-HOURS lines and annotates\nthem LENS-FALSIFIED-c196 inline, so a stale pre-v2.36 fleet file\ncannot re-infect the phrase with the falsified attribution; events\nlines pass verbatim. Belt-tested both shapes in a fixture PDIR\n(BELT-TEST-CONTAMINATION guard held -- I ran it against /tmp, not the\nlive repo). Committed 00eac493, pushed, sophon pulled, live-fire\nverified: the CURRENT-AFFECT fear line now speaks events language.\n\nThe deeper texture: this is the third time an instrument's consumer\nlagged its producer's vocabulary (v1.3 token-pattern grep missed\nJOURNAL-BLIND; the 16:01Z fire quoted hour-dirs post-falsification).\nA lens rename is a CONTRACT between instruments, and the consumer\nside of t...[+6797 chars]
