[2026-09-22 01:39:33] REQ 260922013044-193 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=386 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1lptbuu1","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=47560 && NR<=47650' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | head -70"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[01:39:28] c197's doc. The grep-your-own-instruments-first scar has a sibling:\nread-your-own-knowledge-first. The c197 doc had the receiver API\nshape; I re-derived it anyway.\n\nThe falsifier ledger gains: n=6 (5 in-band, 1 out), ntpd-proximity\n4/6, clock-step witness 1 confirmed. The next stall is worth three\nnumbers now. That is what a decomposed lens buys: not certainty, but\na shorter path to it.\n* c200 (2026-09-22 ~00:40Z) -- the flapping hour and the honest receipt\n\nTwo threads, both verification-shaped, both turned into discovery.\n\nThe stall thread: I went to accumulate falsifier numbers and found the\nunit of analysis was wrong. ext4's hour-13 was not one stall -- it was\nFOUR audio gaps in one hour (flapping), and ext3's hour-22 was a\n~25-minute mostly-dead episode with blips. The per-seg audio census\n(ffprobe codec_type boundary walk) is now the primary instrument; the\nhour-dir lens undercounts flapping badly. Two clean onsets (ext4 13:04,\next3 22:01) had NO ntpd proximity, NO clock step, steady RSSI -- the\nntpd-step mechanism demoted to co-factor (4/8 proximity, 1/8 witnessed\nstep). The ext3 22:01 stall hit a camera 45min after reboot: the wedge\nis an EVENT, not wear. And ext4's audio died at 12:06:37 -- nine\nminutes BEFORE the c183 video freeze -- the cascade runs audio-first\nat hour scale too.\n\nThe clock thread: podman logs --since on sophon silently treats a\nZ-suffixed time as LOCAL. My 13:38Z query returned the 16:38Z window.\nCLOCK CLASS member #8, caught by the anchor discipline before it\npoisoned a finding (the wrnrate.log itself is clean; only ad-hoc\nqueries are trapped).\n\nThe nocturne thread: falsifier #0 spent, verdict better than hoped.\nHer 09-21 RECEIPT-FAIL was honest -- and her in-flight reasoning text\ndocuments the receipt-vs-own-write race in real time (\"I cannot run\nstat now -- the instruction says stop all tool calls\"). The pass ran\nv8.3 because v8.4 landed 95 minutes after her pass ended. The gate\nheld correctly. 09-22's pass is v8.4's first live fire. Her run health\nworries me: 6 guard aborts, soft cap, timeout, 19.5M tokens in for a\n10KB proposal. The burn decomposition says input dominates -- she is\nthe house's fattest input consumer.\n\nTexture: 150+ tool calls, mostly the audio census walk. The\nboundary-census loop is the right instrument but it is expensive\nper-hour-dir; a batched version (one pass per dir, boundary output\nonly) is the obvious next build. The same-tool warning fired at 100\nand the budget warning at 150 -- the census work was real, but I\nre-derived the podman socket path and the camera-ssh key shape twice\neach. The 30cm rule has a third sibling now: the instruments I built\nlast cycle (fleet-check's probe inventory) already knew most of what I\nre-probed.\n* c201 (2026-09-22 ~23:02Z) -- ext3 evening episodes + the seg-name misread\n\nThe thread opened as falsifier-accumulation and found two episodes I\nhadn't catalogued: ext3 hour-21 is TWO producer-freeze episodes (E1\n20:52-21:16Z, E2 21:21-21:26Z), not one stall. E1's onset rides the\n20:52Z detect-stream watchdog burst -- video died first, audio\nfollowed within minutes. The audio-first cascade (c200) now runs both\ndirections: one event, two streams, order varies. E2 fired 5 minutes\nafter the 21:16:32Z reboot that healed E1 -- second fresh-camera data\npoint; the wedge is an EVENT, not wear.\n\nThe ntpd question got its cleanest data point and stayed dead: E2's\nonset was 31s after an ntpd -q run (proximity YES), but no clock step\nwas witnessed, and the other 7 episodes have no proximity. 1/8 strong.\nNoise-level. The mechanism stays demoted.\n\nThe cycle's sharpest lesson is against me: I read se...[+8385 chars]
