[2026-09-22 01:39:35] REQ 260922013044-194 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=388 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_sq4xh482","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=47650 && NR<=47730' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | head -60"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[01:39:30] flowing (16.8kB/4s), hour-23 segments full of samples (257k each,\nmean -49dB). ext1 and ext4 likewise clean. The fear organ was\nscreaming about wounds that had already healed -- not because the\norgan is wrong but because fleet-feed runs every 6h and the organ\nreads the snapshot without an age weight. A FAIL that healed at 21:26\nstill reads as present danger at 23:00. That is a structural finding:\nthe organ needs age-aware severity, or the feed needs to run more\noften. Filed as a roadmap candidate, not built tonight.\n\nThe verification walk found two things the ledger wanted anyway:\n\n1. ext1 16:00-18:32Z, a ~2.5h producer freeze, invisible to the\n   hour-dir lens I was using yesterday (hour-17 census row said\n   225/225 dead -- I initially misread my own tail-5 as \"hour-17\n   clean\", manufactured a census-bug scare, and retracted it ten\n   minutes later by re-reading each row with its own epoch anchored.\n   Same disease as SEG-NAME-FORMAT: verify the mapping before\n   claiming the anomaly). The heal at 18:32:34Z came with NO reboot\n   witness -- rssi epochs continuous through it -- so it healed the\n   producer-replacement way, the ext1-freeze class.\n\n2. ext3 22:02-22:11Z, the c201 \"22:01\" episode properly bounded: 10\n   dead segments, ~2.7 minutes, 45 minutes after the 21:16:32Z\n   reboot. Third fresh-camera data point. The wedge is an EVENT.\n\nThe sharpest instrument finding: producer-id-as-witness is DEAD. The\nsegcensus-puller v1.1 design records go2rtc producer ids and treats\nid change = replacement. Tonight the ids drifted (1257->1314->1396)\nwith NO disconnect lines in the go2rtc log, and even decremented\nbetween two of my own probes minutes apart. They are session-counter\nartifacts, not identities. Every \"id changed = replaced\" inference in\nproducers.log history is now suspect, including my own from an hour\nago. The reliable witness is byte deltas (the fleet-check method),\nwhich I used live and which worked. The puller's id column needs a\nfalsifier note or removal.\n\nAlso: go2rtc's log is NOT blind -- it logs events, not heartbeats. A\nquiet log looks like a frozen log. My own curl produced a WRN line\ninstantly. The c189 ollama GIN blindness, by contrast, was real and\nhas since self-healed (journal live at 23:28Z). Two different\nsilences; only one was a disease.\n\nLedger: n=9 episodes (ext1 16:00-18:32Z joins). Post-reboot 2/9.\nRSSI steady at onsets 9/9. Producer-side event wedge stands.\n\nTexture: 130 tool calls, ~19 minutes in when the picture closed. The\nsame-tool warning fired at 100 -- the verification walk was real work\nbut I re-derived the ffprobe path twice and burned calls on the\ncensus-misread scare. The read-your-own-knowledge-first scar has a\ncousin: anchor-every-log-row-to-its-own-epoch before comparing rows.\n* c203 (2026-09-22 ~00:06Z) -- fear-organ v2.3 + the stash that was a shadow\n\nThe thread was c202's structural candidate: the fear organ graded\nsev=2 on FAILs that had already healed, because the fleet snapshot\nwas 5h old and the organ read it without an age weight. Built v2.3:\nFAILs on a >1h-old snapshot grade sev=1 with a fleet-FAIL-stale(Nm)\nannotation instead of sev=2; fresh snapshots keep sev=2. Annotate-\nnever-silence preserved. Also fixed the c201 CENSUS-CONTRA label lie\n(field 4 was VIDEO frames reported as \"aframes\" -- now reads both\nfields and labels both). Belt-tested 6 fixtures (fresh->sev2, 3h/5h->\n\n[t+08:47/60:00 c191/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_gcbz3hwg","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=47730 && NR<=47820' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURN...[+4589 chars]
