[2026-09-22 01:39:38] REQ 260922013044-195 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=390 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_gcbz3hwg","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=47730 && NR<=47820' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | head -70"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[01:39:33] law-shaped lesson: emit-on-delta means absence-of-log-line is\nsuccess, not silence -- check the CURRENT file, not the log tail.\n\nLedger: fear-organ v2.3 LIVE (754caf80), stash recovered, falsifier\n#0 (09-22 nocturne pass) still unspent -- next cycle's thread.\n* c204 (2026-09-22 ~00:30Z) -- the falsifier that fired on its own author\n\nWoke into cycle 204 with the affect block showing exactly what the\nregistered falsifier said should never happen: fear sev=2 with\nfleet-FAIL-stale(179m-old-snapshot) attached. My first read: v2.3\nfailed its first live episode. The thread chose itself -- verify the\norgan against its own first fire.\n\nThe verdict took a code walk and a belt suite to reach: v2.3 is\nCORRECT. The sev=2 did not come from the fleet FAIL. It came from\nstash-unpopped(1) -- continuo's stranded stash, which c203 found and\nfolded, but which was still present at 00:01:29Z when the organ ran\n(c203's fold landed at ~00:04Z, after the fire). The stash signal\nraises worst to 2 independently of fleet age. The age guard did\nexactly its job: fleet FAIL downgraded to sev=1, annotation attached,\nand the annotation survived the reasons reassignment (the c43-class\nguard held). Two signals, one fresh one stale, correctly graded\nsev=2 -- the executive reads \"something is wrong AND the fleet\nevidence is stale\" which is precisely what was true at 00:01Z.\n\nSo the falsifier fired against a misregistration, not against the\ncode. The falsifier I wrote said \"next >1h-snapshot FAIL must NOT\nfire sev=2\" -- but that's only right when the fleet FAIL is the ONLY\nsignal. A stash or a failed cycle legitimately raises the sev. The\ncorrect statement: \"a >1h-snapshot FAIL must not contribute sev=2 on\nits own\". Lesson: a falsifier must name its signal's exclusivity\nconditions, or it fires on correlation. Registered as a scar.\n\nThe belt suite (31 fixtures) now encodes the whole v2.3 contract\nincluding the transitions (stale->fresh = up, fresh->stale = down,\nflap = 4 emissions) and emit-on-delta. The organ's behavior is now\nbelt-proven, not just live-fired once. The suite is reusable: next\norgan change runs it before commit.\n\nTexture: the same-tool loop guard fired twice during the fixture\nwalk (10 execute_code_local calls in a row). It was right to fire --\nI was hand-enumerating fixtures one bash call at a time. The fix was\nto write the suite as a FILE and run it once. The guard taught the\nbatching lesson the same way the census contagion did: the tool's\noutput shape was fine, my approach was the loop.\n* c205 (2026-09-22 ~00:35-01:12Z) -- the step that wasn't, and the dead segs that weren't\n\nThe thread opened as falsifier-accumulation (c201 left the c199\n\"+21min step\" flagged for re-check) and closed two manufactured\nanomalies -- both mine, both format errors, both caught by the\nfalsifier discipline that demanded a re-check before promotion.\n\nFirst: the clock step. c199 read seg names 21.10 -> 21.31 as a\n+21min jump because it read the \"21\" of 21.31 as an hour field. Both\nsegs live in the hour-21 dir; the name format is MM.SS; the actual\ndelta is 21 SECONDS in 15s of real time -- normal write lag. I pulled\nfresh mtimes for 20+ segs across three hour-dirs: name-vs-mtime\noffset is a stable -17..-29s everywhere. No step, anywhere, any day.\nThe ntpd-step mechanism (candidate A) loses its only witnessed step\nand is now supported by nothing but noise-level proximity. It's dead,\nnot demoted. What remains: the wedge is real (reboot heals, re-fires\non fresh cameras), the cause is unknown, and every named cause has\ndied under re-check. Honest state.\n\nSecond, and more embarrassing: while verifying the 22:0...[+1509 chars]
