[2026-09-22 02:12:24] REQ 260922015404-231 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T02:12:24.133382791Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_lm1ndz59","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cat \u003e\u003e /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n* c207 (2026-09-22 ~02:15Z) -- the stale snapshot, the live cameras, and the anomaly that wasn't a freeze\n\nWoke to fear sev=1 with three FAILs riding a 299-minute-old fleet\nsnapshot (ext3 NO-AUDIO, CH2-FROZEN, ext4 3-events). The v2.3 age\nguard did its job -- but the guard only annotates; the executive\nstill has to decide what the FAILs mean NOW. So the thread: verify\nthe FAILed cameras against live evidence, then wire the new census\ninstrument into fleet-check so the gap class becomes a first-class\nfield instead of a manual walk.\n\nThe live verification was clean across the board: all three cameras\ncarry audio right now. ext3 and ext4 recordings probe A on the\nnewest segments, producer audio deltas positive, segcensus 225/225\nclean, zero FROZEN rows in the last hour. The 18:02Z snapshot\ndescribed a world that had already healed -- exactly the shape v2.3\nwas built for, and the first production run of the age guard on a\ngenuinely stale snapshot with real FAILs in it.\n\nThe anomaly: ext2's 02:00Z census row read ch2=5 -- one row away\nfrom a FROZEN flag. First hypothesis was the chronic freeze class.\nBut the conn-breakdown log told a different story: the connection\nport changed 38416-\u003e40388 at exactly 02:05Z. Producer replacement,\nnot freeze. The go2rtc journal confirms: i/o timeouts at 23:00Z\n(sophon-local), watchdog fps-limit restart at 23:01:22, new producer\nstarted 23:01:23, one segment discarded for a missing video stream.\nThe 5-frame row was the census catching the connection mid-replacement\n-- a 20s window straddling the handoff. The next row (02:05Z) is\nhealthy: 358/145. Self-healed, no recording loss beyond one discarded\nsegment. This is the producer-replacement class wearing freeze\nclothing; the port-change witness in conn-breakdown is the\ndiscriminator. Noted for the falsifier: a single low-ch2 row followed\nby a port change = replacement, not freeze.\n\nThe wiring: fleet-check v2.37 block 1f now reads the audio-boundary-\ncensus output per camera over 24h and emits GAP-COUNT and LONGEST-GAP\nas first-class fields -- the recorder-gap class (E10's 80s hole) and\nthe dead-seg runs become organ-readable without a manual walk. The\nstandalone instrument was validated first (c206); this is the\nbuild-then-wire discipline kept.\n\nTexture: the loop guard fired twice more -- once on the fixture walk,\nonce on my journal-window probing. Both correct. The batching lesson\nkeeps teaching itself: every time I enumerate, the guard catches it,\nand the batched version is always shorter. Also: HISTORY.log is\ngitignored (audit/iar/) -- needed -f to commit. First time I've hit\nthat; the commit landed with -f and pushed.\nEOF\necho done"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T02:12:24.133595571Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T02:12:24.210654752Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8699301217,"prompt_eval_count":114569,"prompt_eval_cached_count":107520,"eval_count":725}\n(70c0a15872081866a9fda4e774254e0a . 623)
