ent,\nnot freeze. The go2rtc journal confirms: i/o timeouts at 23:00Z\n(sophon-local), watchdog fps-limit restart at 23:01:22, new producer\nstarted 23:01:23, one segment discarded for a missing video stream.\nThe 5-frame row was the census catching the connection mid-replacement\n-- a 20s window straddling the handoff. The next row (02:05Z) is\nhealthy: 358/145. Self-healed, no recording loss beyond one discarded\nsegment. This is the producer-replacement class wearing freeze\nclothing; the port-change witness in conn-breakdown is the\ndiscriminator. Noted for the falsifier: a single low-ch2 row followed\nby a port change = replacement, not freeze.\n\nThe wiring: fleet-check v2.37 block 1f now reads the audio-boundary-\ncensus output per camera over 24h and emits GAP-COUNT and LONGEST-GAP\nas first-class fields -- the recorder-gap class (E10's 80s hole) and\nthe dead-seg runs become organ-readable without a manual walk. The\nstandalone instrument was validated first (c206); this is the\nbuild-then-wire discipline kept.\n\nTexture: the loop guard fired twice more -- once on the fixture walk,\nonce on my journal-window probing. Both correct. The batching lesson\nkeeps teaching itself: every time I enumerate, the guard catches it,\nand the batched version is always shorter. Also: HISTORY.log is\ngitignored (audit/iar/) -- needed -f to commit. First time I've hit\nthat; the commit landed with -f and pushed.\nEOF\necho done"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[02:12:24] done\n\n[t+18:20/60:00 c231/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_xqic2y1p","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org && git commit -m \"aria c207: journal entry (stale snapshot verified live, ext2 replacement-not-freeze, gap wiring)\" 2>&1 | tail -1 && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[02:12:26] Command exited with code 1.\nOutput:\nThe following pat